BND-12: count TIMEOPEN / TIMECLOSED from the start of the run, not from midnight

link_initState() set every link's timeLastSet to StartDate, the date part
of the start (midnight), so TIMEOPEN / TIMECLOSED rule premises and the
toolkit's swmm_LINK_TIMEOPEN / swmm_LINK_TIMECLOSED values included the
start time of day: in a run starting at 06:00 every link had been open or
closed for 6 h at the first step. Use StartDateTime.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-12_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/link.c b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
index 31925e1..43a26ce 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/link.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
@@ -526,7 +526,7 @@ void link_initState(int j)
     Link[j].newVolume = 0.0;
     Link[j].setting   = 1.0;
     Link[j].targetSetting = 1.0;
-    Link[j].timeLastSet = StartDate;
+    Link[j].timeLastSet = StartDateTime;
     Link[j].inletControl  = FALSE;
     Link[j].normalFlow    = FALSE;
     if ( Link[j].type == CONDUIT ) conduit_initState(j, Link[j].subIndex);
